1. **What was failing and why:** The three failing tests all involve `-p -m MODE existing_dir` where the target directory already exists. The code was unconditionally calling `chmod` on the final directory after `create_parents` succeeded, but `create_parents` treats an existing directory as success (EEXIST → continue). This caused the mode of pre-existing directories to be overwritten.

